    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d566">

                <pb facs="0589" n="577" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg577"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.24546/10: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister to the Netherlands Government in Exile</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Biddle</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-10-22T18:00:00+01:00">October 22, 1941—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 22—2:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Netherlands Series 31. Your Netherlands Series 32, October 15, 7 p.m.<anchor
                        n="8" xml:id="d566-f1"/> and 33, October 20, 1 p.m.<anchor n="9"
                        xml:id="d566-f2"/> Following is body of letter of today’s date received from
                    Foreign Minister Van Kleffens:<anchor n="10" xml:id="d566-f3"/>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“It has been arranged between the Minister for the Colonies and myself
                            that a telegram be sent today to the Governor General of the Netherlands
                            Indies in order to authorize J. H. R. Van Starkenborg to cause contact
                            to be made forthwith with the Commander in Chief in Manila in case the
                            Governor General sees no objection on his part to acceding to the
                            desires of your Government in the matter of making air bases in the
                            Netherlands Indies available for the purpose of ferrying heavy American
                            bombers from Hawaii to the Philippine Islands.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">Biddle</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d566-f1" n="8" xml:id="d566-f1-content">
                <p>See last paragraph of telegram No. 4458, October 15, 7 p.m., to the Ambassador in
                    the United Kingdom, <ref target="#pg573">p. 573</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d566-f2" n="9" xml:id="d566-f2-content">
                <p>See footnote 6, <ref target="#pg576">p. 576</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d566-f3" n="10" xml:id="d566-f3-content">
                <p>Eelco Nicolaas van Kleffens, Netherland Foreign Minister.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
